coder › Implemented `toc(markdown)` in `src/toc.ts` and added tests in `src/toc.test.ts`.

What changed
- `src/toc.ts`
  - Added an ATX heading regex `^(#{1,6}) (.*)$` (1–6 `#` then a literal space).
  - Splits on `\r?\n`, tracks ``` fences (any line starting with ``` toggles), and skips headings inside them.
  - `text` is the part after the marker, `.trim()`ed.
  - `slug` lowercases, collapses runs of non-letters/digits to one dash, and trims dashes from both ends.
  - Duplicate slugs reuse a `Set`: first stays as-is, later ones get `-2`, `-3`, … (skipping any that already exist).
- `src/toc.test.ts`
  - 9 tests covering levels 1–6, non-headings (`#no-space`, 7 `#`s), whitespace trimming, slug generation, duplicate slugs, headings inside fences, fences with info strings/extra backticks, CRLF endings, and the empty `# ` heading.

Decisions the request didn't spell out
- Headings are recognized only at the start of a line (no indented headings), matching the literal “one to six # characters followed by a space”.
- “Letters or digits” is treated as ASCII `[a-z0-9]` after lowercasing (the classic slug behavior).
- Closing `#` sequences (e.g. `## Title ##`) are kept as text, since only the opening marker was specified.

